                        "entry_id": "c5399649-319f-3c6d-b3db-b3fa507c9625",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An organic compound, C₈H₇N, found in coal tar, and produced in the gut by the bacterial decomposition of tryptophan; it is an aromatic bicyclic heterocycle having a benzene ring fused with a pyrrole ring; indole and its derivatives occur widely in nature and have many industrial applications."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8022fd1a-7d3b-4ec9-b8d0-dee7b2b0a830",
                                "sense_id": "98466f1c-446d-39b8-a80d-cff9bb1f5d54",
                                "text": "The Aspidosperma alkaloids are the largest group of indole alkaloids."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "06f6d953-3a06-44d1-88cf-8bb7bf2a0bab",
                                "sense_id": "98466f1c-446d-39b8-a80d-cff9bb1f5d54",
                                "text": "Intakes of indoles or their parental glucosinolates, may have beneficial health effects as well as toxicological effects."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9b43d601-c768-30fd-818e-6ff527009d2c",
                        "entry_id": "c5399649-319f-3c6d-b3db-b3fa507c9625",
